  "_exec_summary": [
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000120198,
      "SummaryText": "The following is a summary of the six elements of the Risk Management Program as part of our 5-year update that has been implemented at the Harcros facility located at 4280 Rifle Range Road, Vicksburg, MS 39180. The changes in this RMP update include the recently updated PHA, which has formatting changes and a more detailed human factors review. The RMP also includes several updated dates and an updated executive summary.\n\n1. Accidental release prevention and emergency response policies\nOur emergency response program is a detailed response plan for any releases/exposures to chlorine and sulfur dioxide. The site does have HAZWOPER trained employees. The emergency response plan includes procedures for notification of the local fire authority and notification of our immediate neighbors.\n\n2. Stationary source and regulated substances handled\nThe facility handles two chemicals above the RMP threshold limits: Chlorine and Sulfur Dioxide The chlorine is stored in 150 lb and 2,000 lb cylinders.  The sulfur dioxide is stored in 150 lb cylinders. The chemical is neither packaged or used at this facility.\n\n3. Accidental release prevention program\nDue to the storage and handling of chlorine and sulfur dioxide, this site falls under RMP Program Level 3. An original Process Hazard Analysis was conducted and those corrective actions have been closed. The facility revalidated the Process Hazard Analysis in December, 2024 and all corrective actions were completed by October, 2025. The accidental release prevention program includes, but is not limited to, access control and security of the site; checking prepackaged containers that cross their docks for tampering and damage, as per the standard operating procedure, and emergency response.\n\n4. 5-Year accident history\nNo RMP process-related accidents have occurred at this facility within the last five years.\n\n5. Emergency Response program\nThe facility's emergency response is outlined in their specific Emergency Action and Emergency Res"
    },
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 1,
      "FacilityID": 1000120198,
      "SummaryText": "ponse Plans which includes responding to chlorine and sulfur dioxide releases, onsite only. The Harcros team members that handle the RMP chemicals are HAZWOPER. Harcros works closely with our suppliers, customers, and public responders to continuously improve our emergency response capabilities.\n\n6. Planned changes to improve safety\nHarcros continues to participate in the Alliance for Chemical Distribution (ACD) programs, and although no specific safety improvements are scheduled at this time, we continue to improve our operations in accordance\nwith Responsible Distribution Guidelines. Frequent site inspections and audits are completed in order to identify any safety improvements needed."
    }
